{
  "id": "north-brunswick-hurricane",
  "name": "North Brunswick Hurricane Landfall",
  "description": "Major-hurricane wind and rain bands crossing Middlesex County, NJ, centred on the Township of North Brunswick. 30 nodes covering the PSE&G assets feeding the township (the Brunswick 230kV switching station on Victory Avenue and the 69kV sub-transmission tier at 14th Street, Adams and Bennetts Lane), four real receiving facilities in New Brunswick and Piscataway, the Township's three volunteer fire companies plus its separate First Aid & Rescue Squad, and three adjacent volunteer departments. The Township Municipal Building on Hermann Road acts as the township-level emergency operations centre; the county's Emergency Services Center is in Sayreville, outside the township. North Brunswick Township and the City of New Brunswick are adjacent but separate municipalities with their own fire, EMS and OEM, so the hospitals here are City of New Brunswick facilities reached by mutual aid. Substation names, street addresses and coordinates come from the Township of North Brunswick directory, RWJBarnabas Health, NJDEP permit NJG0306801, PSE&G/PJM planning filings and OpenStreetMap; tower and mesh-relay sites are modelled on real corridors, and the coverage they provide is modelled, not measured.",
  "hazardModel": "MAJOR_HURRICANE",
  "tickMinutes": 5,
  "startHour": 6,
  "startMinute": 15,
